> I’m organizing the Connectathon Talks for Connectathon 2014.
>
> Unlike the testing floor, these talks are open to the public, and will be held in the upstairs conference room in the Mellon Auditorium, as in years past.  The talks are held Tuesday and Wednesday afternoons during Connectathon 2014.  Appropriate topics are technical talks on areas that are of broad interest to the NFS community.
>
> If you are interested in presenting a talk, please send me:
>
>   o  A presentation title
>   o  A 2-4 sentence abstract of the presentation
>   o  The name and e-mail addresses of all presenters.  I will not share these with anyone
>   o  How long you need: typically 30 or 60 minutes
>
> A VGA overhead projector is available.
>
> This year, in addition to presentations by individuals, I’d like to host several “birds of a feather” sessions where we can hold group discussion on topics relevant to our community.  These sessions would be held during one or more of the normal talk slots (Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon), and would be open to the public.  I have a few BOF sessions in mind already:
>
>   o  NFS Testing (a perennial favorite)
>   o  NFS/Kerberos
>   o  NFS/RDMA
>   o  NFS-Ganesha
>   o  Linux libtirpc
>
> Please send suggestions.
>
> A schedule of talks and BOF sessions will be posted on the connectathon.info web site as we get closer to the event.
